    {
      "id": "far-cf-deposit-expense-receivable-c2",
      "heading": "Transaction 5: an advertisement is an expense",
      "explanation_md": "Circle Films **pays ₹250 cash to run an ad in the local paper.**\n\nCash falls, so assets decrease. A decrease in assets from **operating a business is an expense**. Expenses decrease net income and therefore retained earnings, so **equity decreases**.\n\nTable: Cash ₹8,500 - ₹250 = ₹8,250; Retained Earnings ₹1,500 - ₹250 = ₹1,250. Total assets ₹18,250 = Liabilities ₹2,000 + Equity ₹16,250.",
      "example_ids": [
        "far-ex-t5-ad"
      ],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Expense",
          "meaning": "A decrease in assets from operating a business; it lowers net income and retained earnings.",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#2"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "Paying an expense in cash lowers cash and retained earnings by the same amount.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
