    {
      "id": "far-cf-deposit-expense-receivable-q-863d4637",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Analyse transactions 4, 5 and 6 of Circle Films on the accounting equation, showing the totals after each.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "Starting position (after transaction 3): Cash ₹6,500, Supplies ₹1,000, Equipment ₹9,000; Common Stock ₹15,000, Retained Earnings ₹1,500.\n\n**Transaction 4: ₹2,000 deposit.** Cash +₹2,000 (₹8,500). Unearned Revenue +₹2,000 because the service is still owed. Assets ₹18,500 = Liabilities ₹2,000 + Equity ₹16,500.\n\n**Transaction 5: ₹250 ad.** Cash -₹250 (₹8,250). The expense reduces retained earnings to ₹1,250. Assets ₹18,250 = ₹2,000 + ₹16,250.\n\n**Transaction 6: dance competition, ₹3,500 invoice.** Accounts Receivable +₹3,500. Revenue raises retained earnings to ₹4,750. Assets ₹21,750 = ₹2,000 + ₹19,750.\n\nThe equation balances throughout.",
      "rubric": [
        {
          "point": "Transaction 4 effects and totals",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#2"
        },
        {
          "point": "Transaction 5 as an expense",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#2"
        },
        {
          "point": "Transaction 6 as receivable and revenue",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#2"
        },
        {
          "point": "Totals 18,500, 18,250, 21,750",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#2"
        },
        {
          "point": "Balance each time",
